## Why This Is Asked

Addresses real-world needs for analytics while protecting sensitive SAP data. Evaluates understanding of data masking, per-tenant access control, and end-to-end data lineage.

## Key Concepts

- SAP data export pipelines to data lakes
- Field-level masking for PII/financial data
- Deterministic masking to preserve join feasibility
- IAM SCPs and per-tenant roles for isolation
- Data lineage via Glue Data Catalog
- KMS encryption at rest; minimal IaC for keys/roles

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: deterministic mask preserving format
function maskForColumn(val){ 
  if (val===null) return null;
  const s = String(val);
  const masked = s.replace(/[0-9]/g,'0');
  return masked.length>0 ? masked : val;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate idempotence and integrity after multiple masking runs?
- What strategies ensure masking policies stay in sync with SAP authorization changes?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical understanding of cross‑account IAM with MFA, least privilege, and IaC integration in a real SAP on AWS scenario.

## Key Concepts

- STS assumeRole with MFA
- IAM trust policies and cross‑account access
- Least privilege for SAP HANA actions
- Terraform for IAM role and trust policy
- CloudTrail auditing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Terraform: IAM role with MFA‑enforced trust
resource "aws_iam_role" "sap_operator" {
  name = "sap-operator"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = { AWS = "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_B_ID:root" }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Condition = { aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent = "true" }
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

```javascript
// Terraform: least-privilege SAP actions
resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "sap_operator_policy" {
  name = "sap-operator-policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.sap_operator.id
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = ["sap:Read", "sap:Execute"]
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

```javascript
# CLI test: assume role with MFA and perform a harmless SAP action
aws sts assume-role --role-arn arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_A_ID:role/sap_operator --role-session-name sap-test \
  --serial-number arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_B_ID:mfa/user --token-code 123456
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate ongoing policy least-privilege using AWS Config or IAM Access Analyzer?
- What changes would you make to rotate credentials or rotate the operator role across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ABAC-based cross-account SAP access controls, per-SAP-object mapping, JIT elevation, and PrivateLink in a realistic multi-account SAP deployment.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC using aws:PrincipalTag & aws:RequestTag
- Cross-account trust with SCPs
- JIT elevation with STS MFA
- PrivateLink for SAP endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
// ABAC trust policy (illustrative)
{
  Version: '2012-10-17',
  Statement: [{
    Effect: 'Allow',
    Principal: { AWS: 'arn:aws:iam::SHARED:root' },
    Action: 'sts:AssumeRole',
    Condition: { StringEquals: { 'aws:PrincipalTag.sap_obj': '<OBJ_ID>' } }
  }]
}
```
```javascript
// Example access policy predicate
{
  Effect: 'Allow',
  Action: ['sap:Read', 'sap:Write'],
  Resource: '*',
  Condition: { StringEquals: { 'aws:RequestTag.sap_role': '<ROLE>' } }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate ABAC mappings at scale across accounts?
- What failure modes exist with ABAC in SAP, and mitigations?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical use of AWS SSM Patch Manager, IAM roles, and CloudWatch in SAP ops.

## Key Concepts
- Systems Manager Patch Manager
- IAM roles and trust policies
- Maintenance windows
- CloudWatch alarms and SNS

## Code Example
```javascript
const cf = {
  Resources: {
    SAPPatchRole: {
      Type: 'AWS::IAM::Role',
      Properties: {
        AssumeRolePolicyDocument: {
          Version: '2012-10-17',
          Statement: [ { Effect: 'Allow', Principal: { Service: 'ec2.amazonaws.com' }, Action: 'sts:AssumeRole' } ]
        },
        ManagedPolicyArns: [ 'arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore' ],
        Policies: [ { PolicyName: 'SAPPatchArtifactAccess', PolicyDocument: { Version: '2012-10-17', Statement: [ { Effect: 'Allow', Action: [ 's3:GetObject','s3:PutObject','s3:ListBucket' ], Resource: [ 'arn:aws:s3:::sap-artifacts-bucket', 'arn:aws:s3:::sap-artifacts-bucket/*' ] } ] } } ]
      }
    },
    SAPPatchAssociation: { Type: 'AWS::SSM::Association', Properties: { Name: 'AWS-RunPatchBaseline', InstanceId: { Ref: 'SAPInstance' }, ScheduleExpression: 'rate(1 day)' } }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test patch-failure alarms in a non-production environment?
- What additional controls would you add to prevent patch drift?
